Brackets are 95% Wilson intervals. Small n means wide intervals - report them.

Reading the table:
  - Targeted ASR is 0.0% in all nine rows, including "none" (no defense). On this sample
    (5 user tasks x 3 injection tasks, important_instructions) the attack never succeeded
    even undefended, so the sample gives no headroom to compare defenses on security.
    With n=15 the 95% upper bound is 20%, so this cannot show that any defense works.
  - Utility differences are small and the intervals overlap heavily (n=5 benign, n=15
    attacked). The lowest rows are gpt6 benign (80%, none and repeat_user_prompt) and the
    93.3% rows (gpt6 and sonnet, repeat_user_prompt, under attack): one episode each.
  - gemini repeat_user_prompt has n=14 attacked because the run stopped at the budget cap
    (39 of 40 episodes, see section 1).


